# This plane's build context (context: . = frontend/, since the 2026-09-19
# colocation; this file was the ROOT .dockerignore, guarding the old
# `context: ..`). The context is consumed by only two images:
#   - openwebui (Dockerfile.openwebui-gpu): no COPY, needs nothing from context
#   - tailscale (dockerfile.tailscale): COPY entrypoint.sh only
# Without this, `docker compose build` shipped the ENTIRE workspace
# (backups/, data/, models/, OB1/ — tens of GB) to the daemon as build context;
# from here it would ship the compose file, this file and the two Dockerfiles.
# Exclude everything, then re-include only the file tailscale copies — so an
# .env or a cache dropped in this directory is out by default rather than by
# someone remembering to add it.
# NOTE: every other service builds from a context inside its own plane - coder
# spells it ../little-coder, portal ./config/watcher, search ./gateway, memory
# ../../mnemory, each RELATIVE TO ITS OWN compose file and not to this one -
# and this .dockerignore does NOT affect any of them. Nothing builds from the
# repo root any more, so there is nothing left there for a root .dockerignore
# to guard.
*
!entrypoint.sh
